// How Cloudflare serves the planner.
//
// The site is a Worker with static assets rather than a Pages project — that is
// what "Connect to Git" builds now. It runs `npx wrangler deploy` from the
// repository root on every push to main, so this file is what it obeys. Without
// it committed, Wrangler guesses a fresh config on each build.
//
// `name` is load-bearing: it is the deployed Worker, and changing it creates a
// second one on a different address. Leave it alone unless you also update the
// Site URL and Redirect URLs in Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration.
//
// What actually gets uploaded is this directory minus .assetsignore's list.
// `_headers` is read by Cloudflare and applied to responses; it is not served.
//
// The keep-alive ping is a separate Worker with its own config in worker/. It is
// not deployed by this build — run `npx wrangler deploy` inside worker/ once.
{
  "name": "wedding-command-and-control",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-11",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "."
  },
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
